Overlay patch 0053: the PSVR2 Sense fixed layout's pad seam, and MK64's armed
item (VR-spec D13/D9, VR R4).

Two edits, both tiny, both in game code that already had exactly the hook the
feature needed:

  1. src/main.c — `read_controllers()`. Straight after `osContGetReadData()`
     fills gControllerPads and BEFORE `update_controller(0)` derives the
     pressed/depressed edges from it, the shell ORs the Sense pair's fixed
     kart layout onto player 1's pad. This is the whole reason the layout is
     "deliberately not a user bind" (spec D9): there is no LUS binding layer
     between a Sense button and its N64 bit — the bits are written straight into
     the pad MK64 is about to read, and MK64's own edge detection then runs over
     the merged state, so a Sense press produces exactly the same buttonPressed /
     buttonDepressed edges a real N64 controller would (trap C2: ONE edge
     detector, and it is the game's).

     ORed, never assigned: a gamepad and the Sense pair can drive the same kart
     at once, which is what makes a headset session recoverable if the Sense
     layout ever misbehaves (the donor's 1.1.2.22 lesson — never leave the
     headset with no working input).

  2. src/racing/actors_extended.c — `check_player_use_item()`. Exports player
     1's armed item as gSohVRItemArmed. That is the state the "item in hand"
     billboard is gated on, the edge the item-pickup haptic fires from, and the
     thing that tells the throw gesture whether there is anything to throw. The
     site runs once per player every frame the item logic ticks, and it is
     placed at the TOP of the loop body rather than inside the
     `prevent_item_use` / HUMAN / non-NONE guard, so the export tracks the real
     state (including "you have nothing") rather than only the frames where a
     use would have been legal.

The shell entry point is `SohVRSense_WritePad` in SohIosShell.m — the same seam
discipline patch 0023 rev5's settings rows use: src/main.c is C compiled on
EVERY target (iPhone, visionOS and the macOS build), SohSense.m is visionOS-only
(patch 0013's target_sources), so the game calls a forwarder that every target
compiles and only the visionOS build forwards anything. __IOS__-guarded, so the
oracle links no shell and is byte-identical to upstream.


